#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059426 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0de0627b-2568-5c02-8928-d14344df5a2f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of an Expression With Sine or Cosine Trigonometric Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "31b9e2d8-1458-50b3-a920-703476825420" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-3631" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $y = 3\\cos x + 4\\sin x + 2x^3$." :question/worked-solution "We know that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x} (\\sin x) = \\cos x\n$$\n\nand that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x} (\\cos x) = -\\sin x\n$$\n\nApplying these formulas, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{d}{dx}(3\\cos x + 4\\sin x + 2x^{3}) \\\\\n&= 3\\frac{d}{dx}(\\cos x) + 4\\frac{d}{dx}(\\sin x) + 2\\frac{d}{dx}(x^{3}) \\\\\n&=-3\\sin x + 4\\cos x + 2(3)x^{2} \\\\\n&=-3\\sin x + 4\\cos x + 6x^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059427 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "711f198b-26b4-5185-812a-102329d49313" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of an Expression With the Tangent Trigonometric Function"}] :question/id #uuid "ae922c00-2ff5-5a46-805a-62955bc5a08a" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-3632" :question/problem "Find the slope of $y = 4\\tan x + 5x$ at $x = 0$." :question/worked-solution "The slope at $x=0$ is given by the value of the derivative $y'$ at $x=0$.\n\nFirst, we compute the derivative, using the fact that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x} (\\tan x) = \\sec^2 x\n$$\n\nWe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^{′}(x) &= \\frac{d}{dx}(4\\tan x + 5x) \\\\\n&= 4\\sec^{2} x + 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=0$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^{′}(0) &= 4\\sec^{2} 0 + 5 \\\\\n&= 4 \\cdot 1 + 5 \\\\\n&= 9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope is $9$."}]}
